Abstract: This study systematically investigates the pollution hazards and the current status and requirements of environ⁃
mental risk management of toxic and hazardous chemicals in auxiliary materials for shield tunneling both domestically and
internationally. In response to the current issues in China, such as the lack of environmental management for chemical aux⁃
iliary materials in shield tunneling, the lag in environmental risk prevention and control, and the insufficiency in technical
support capabilities, the study proposes suggestions for strengthening the environmental risk management of chemical auxil⁃
iary materials in shield tunneling, oriented by the national needs for environmental and health risk management. These sug⁃
gestions include screening a list of high⁃volume, high⁃hazard chemical substances used in shield tunneling, assessing the
environmental risks of substances on the list, establishing a green access model to prevent pollution at its source, and clar⁃
ifying the classification methods and treatment requirements for shield tunneling muck and to implement classified manage⁃
ment of muck. This study will effectively support the construction of green rail transit projects and provide theoretical meth⁃
ods and data for the government to formulate the environmental management policy of shield tunneling.
Key words: shield tunneling auxiliary materials; toxic and hazardous chemicals; environmental risk; management sug⁃
gestions
